2.2. General Methods. Thermogravimetric analyses (TGA) were performed on a Netzsch TG 209 instrument in flowing ${\bf N}_{2}$ at a heating rate of $10~^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ per minute in the range of 25 to $600~^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ . PXRD measurements were performed on a Bruker D8 ADVANCE X-ray diffractometer with $\mathrm{Cu-K}_{\alpha}$ radiation. PXRD measurements at different temperatures were recorded after the sample had been kept at the respective temperature for $20\ \mathrm{\min}$ in flowing $\Nu_{2}$ . The crystalline powder samples were prepared by crushing the single crystals, and scans of $3\mathrm{-}60^{\circ}$ at a rate of $5^{\circ}/\mathrm{min}$ were recorded. Calculated PXRD patterns were generated using Mercury 3.0.17 Raman spectra were obtained using a Renishaw inVia Raman microscope equipped with a $785~\mathrm{nm}$ diode laser and a 1200 lines/mm grating. The $\mathbf{N}_{2}$ sorption isotherm was recorded with an automatic volumetric adsorption apparatus (IGA-003 series, Hiden Isochema Ltd.) at $77~\mathrm{~K~}.$ The benzene and methanol vapor sorption measurements were performed using a Belsorp-Max automatic volumetric adsorption apparatus. The high-pressure gas sorption measurements were performed using the Belsorp HP-60 high-pressure sorption system. Magnetizations of polycrystalline samples were measured in the temperature range of $2.0{-}300~\mathrm{K}$ and field range $\pm50\mathrm{kOe}$ using a Quantum Design MPMS XL-5 SQUID magnetometer.
2.3. X-ray Diffraction. For the crystal structure determination, single crystals of 1·3DMF, $\mathbf{1}{\cdot}6\mathrm{CH}_{3}\mathrm{OH}$ , $\scriptstyle1\cdot3\mathrm{PrOH},$ and $\mathrm{\mathbf{1}}{\cdot}2\mathrm{C}_{6}\mathrm{H}_{6}$ were selected from batches covered with solvent and fixed to glass fiber for diffraction data collection at $173\mathrm{K}$ However, for guest free 1, the data were collected at $298\mathrm{~K~}$ using the crystal of $\Gamma{\cdot}6\mathrm{CH}_{3}\mathrm{OH}$ after the methanol was removed by heating the crystal at $355\mathrm{~K~}$ for $^\textrm{\scriptsize1h}$ on the diffractometer.
